Improve depth and visual cohesion while keeping the existing Three.js renderer stable.

- Use coherent physically based material values where appropriate: metalness, roughness, surface variation, and emissive response should distinguish metal, painted surfaces, glass, rubber, ceramic, and energy.
- Verify the renderer's color-space and tone-mapping behavior. Follow the project's existing rendering choices unless a measured and visible correction is needed. Consult the official Three.js color-management guidance if appropriate: https://threejs.org/manual/pages/color-management.html
