# Workstream C — Tests and real browser verification

## C1. Simulation and regression tests

Keep all existing tests passing, including the reported tests 1–37. Add tests for every new bug discovered.

At minimum, cover:

1. Echo Heavy marks at the intended contact time, not action-start time.
2. Playback crossing a contact timestamp between simulation updates.
3. Clip ends before contact; no artificial contact occurs.
4. No target in range, target outside the attack arc, and target hidden behind a solid obstacle.
5. Deterministic target selection when multiple eligible enemies are present.
6. Each event executes once per playback, with correct behavior on a new playback.
7. Echo contact never causes HP damage, posture, stagger, knockback, or Flux generation.
8. A pre-mark attack cannot retroactively Converge.
9. Light combo hits 1 and 2 never Converge; the valid Heavy and finisher can.
10. Wrong target, missed hit, expired mark, dead target, and invalid target state do not cause successful Convergence.
11. An existing mark does not get refreshed by later Echo events.
12. Successful Convergence applies normal live-hit damage once and +22 posture through the existing pipeline, with no separate +18 HP bonus.
13. Bastion guard, enemy-specific defensive logic, armor, poise, and stagger thresholds still work correctly.
14. Flux cost and cooldown are each applied once and only on a successful Convergence.
15. Insufficient Flux, Relay interaction, cooldown, and attack-start timing remain correct.
16. Pause/resume, clear, restart, defeat, and victory produce clean lifecycle behavior.
17. Existing puzzle stages, barriers, Echo-only pressure plates, receiver logic, and Relay path blocking remain unchanged.
18. The combat spam-only test still does not trivially outperform the intended skillful play pattern.

Run the project's actual test command, type checking, and production build. Report the real totals and failures; do not lower or delete a test merely to get a green result.

## C2. Live desktop browser checks

Use the existing browser/Playwright workflow with real keyboard and UI interactions. Read-only game telemetry is acceptable for verification, but do not mutate the world directly to fake successful gameplay.

Run at least these scenarios:

- Record and replay an Echo Heavy; observe the mark only when the attack reaches contact.
- Perform a fresh valid Heavy follow-up against the same target and verify one normal hit, +22 posture, one 15-Flux expenditure, one cooldown start, and mark consumption.
- Repeat with an attack started before the mark; prove it cannot retroactively Converge.
- Hit the wrong enemy, miss the target, and let the mark expire; verify no successful effect.
- Test the exact clip/contact boundary and a playback frame that crosses the contact timestamp.
- Place a solid obstacle between Echo and target; verify there is no prime through the obstacle.
- Check Bastion frontal defense and the relevant enemy recovery/stagger outcomes.
- Exercise Relay during an active resonance window and ensure it does not duplicate or clear valid state.
- Verify C/R cleanup, pause/resume, and that repeated inputs cannot spend Flux multiple times.
- Confirm the resonance UI text is correctly separated and its displayed state matches simulation telemetry.
- Check console errors and runtime errors.

## C3. Actual mobile interaction checks

At 390×844, perform a real touch-control sequence where supported by the existing HUD:

- Record and play an Echo.
- Trigger the supported live follow-up using actual mobile buttons.
- Verify the resonance state and cooldown update.
- Verify controls are clickable, do not overlap, and do not obscure the necessary gameplay area.
