## Definition of done

Phase 5.1 is complete only when:

- Convergence no longer has arbitrary bonus HP damage or unconditional defense bypass.
- Contact timing, target identity, mark expiration, Flux expenditure, cooldowns, and state cleanup are covered by passing tests.
- The relevant desktop browser happy paths and failure paths have been exercised.
- Actual mobile controls work for the supported resonance flow.
- The existing game still builds and its previous regression tests pass.
- The Test Bay looks visibly more detailed and cohesive.
- Sera, enemies, Echo, weapons, and combat effects show more convincing layered motion and impact feedback.
- Visual changes do not compromise gameplay readability, deterministic simulation, control responsiveness, or mobile performance.
- The final report lists changed files, important design decisions, test/build results, browser scenarios actually completed, visual validation evidence, known limitations, and any remaining issues.

Do not report completion just because the effects were implemented or all unit tests pass. If any requirement remains unverified, clearly label it as unverified and explain why.

**After this phase is genuinely complete, the next planned milestone is Phase 6: HELIX-04 boss prototype**, built on the verified Convergence system and improved visual foundation. Do not implement Phase 6 as part of this task.